course: dictionary
lesson: 10748
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word urchin is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Sea urchins are covered with movable spines that point towards a threat.» The word sea is the clue: this urchin is an animal that lives in the sea.
explain: In old stories, an urchin means something different. A street urchin is a poor, cheeky child who lives on the streets of an old city. The clue is the word street, and the old-fashioned feel of the story.
explain: The words next to urchin tell you which meaning to use. Sea urchin and street urchin both end in urchin, but the first word changes the meaning. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: An urchin can mean a small sea animal, or a poor, cheeky child in an old story.
fact: A sea urchin is small and round, with a hard shell covered in sharp spines.
fact: Sea urchins eat kelp seaweed, and sea otters eat sea urchins.
fact: Sea urchins live on the sea floor and in rock pools.
fact: Stepping on an urchin's spines hurts, so wear water shoes on rocks.
exercise: «Sea urchins are covered with movable spines that point towards a threat.» What is a sea urchin? | *A small, round sea animal with a hard shell | A poor child who lives on the streets | A boat that sails on the sea | A kind of seaweed
exercise: Ella reads, «The street urchin ran off with the bread.» What is an urchin here? | A small sea animal with sharp spines | A fish that lives in kelp | *A poor, cheeky child who lives on the streets | A rock pool with no animals
exercise: «Sea otters eat sea urchins, which eat kelp.» What do sea urchins eat? | Sea otters | Rocks | *Kelp seaweed | Bread from the street
test: Why is wearing water shoes on rocks a good idea? | To stop sea otters seeing you | To help you run faster | *Because stepping on an urchin's spines hurts | To keep your feet warm
test: In «sea urchin», what does the word sea tell you? | That the urchin is poor | That the urchin is very old | That the urchin lives on the streets | *That the urchin is an animal that lives in the sea
exam: In a story about «the street urchin», which clue tells you urchin means a child, not a sea animal? | *The word street, and the setting of an old city story | The word spines | The word kelp | The word sea
